<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Moree</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Moree is a fishing town on the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a>'s Central Region, a few kilometres east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-coast">Cape Coast</a>. It was the port of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fante">Fante</a> kingdom of Asebu, whose rulers invited the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> to trade there, and in 1612 the Dutch built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-nassau-gold-coast">Fort Nassau</a> at Moree, their first fortified post on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gold-coast">Gold Coast</a>, which served as their headquarters until they took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elmina">Elmina</a> in 1637.</p></div>
